{"id":"mahabharata-8-054","work":"mahabharata","part":8,"partName":"कर्णपर्व","partNameEn":"Karna Parva","unit":54,"title":"चतुःपञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 54 · Bhima's resolve to kill the Kauravas","summary":{"en":"Bhima, surrounded by many foes, rouses his charioteer Vishoka and says he will kill the sons of Dhritarashtra that day. Vishoka praises him and Bhima rewards the news that Arjuna is near.","kn":"ಅನೇಕ ಶತ್ರುಗಳಿಂದ ಸುತ್ತುವರಿಯಲ್ಪಟ್ಟ ಭೀಮ ಸಾರಥಿ ವಿಶೋಕನನ್ನು ಪ್ರೇರಿಸಿ ಅಂದೇ ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರನ ಮಕ್ಕಳನ್ನು ಕೊಲ್ಲುವೆನೆನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ. ವಿಶೋಕ ಅವನನ್ನು ಹೊಗಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಅರ್ಜುನ ಸಮೀಪದಲ್ಲಿದ್ದಾನೆಂಬ ಸುದ್ದಿಗೆ ಭೀಮ ಬಹುಮಾನ ನೀಡುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"अनेक शत्रुओं से घिरे भीम सारथी विशोक को प्रेरित करते हैं और कहते हैं कि वे उसी दिन धृतराष्ट्र के पुत्रों को मारेंगे। विशोक उनकी प्रशंसा करता है और भीम अर्जुन के निकट होने की खबर पर पुरस्कार देते हैं।","te":"అనేక శత్రువులచే చుట్టుముట్టబడిన భీముడు సారథి విశోకుని పురికొల్పి ఆ రోజే ధృతరాష్ట్ర పుత్రులను చంపుతానంటాడు. విశోకుడు అతన్ని పొగుడుతాడు; అర్జునుడు సమీపంలో ఉన్నాడనే వార్తకు భీముడు బహుమతి ఇస్తాడు.","ta":"பல பகைவரால் சூழப்பட்ட பீமன் தேரோட்டி விசோகனை ஊக்கி அன்றே திருதராஷ்டிரனின் மக்களைக் கொல்வதாகக் கூறுகிறான். விசோகன் அவனைப் புகழ, அர்ஜுனன் அருகில் இருக்கிறான் என்ற செய்திக்குப் பீமன் பரிசளிக்கிறான்.","ml":"അനേകം ശത്രുക്കൾക്കിടയിൽ നിൽക്കുന്ന ഭീമൻ, തന്റെ സാരഥി വിശോകനെ ഉണർത്തി, അന്ന് ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രപുത്രന്മാരെ കൊല്ലുമെന്ന് പറയുന്നു. വിശോകൻ അദ്ദേഹത്തെ പ്രശംസിക്കുന്നു; അർജുനൻ അടുത്തുണ്ടെന്ന വാർത്തയ്ക്ക് ഭീമൻ പ്രതിഫലം നൽകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 8.54; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 29 2019","sections":[{"title":"कर्णपर्व","titleEn":"Karna Parva","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"अथ त्विदानीं तुमुले विमर्दे\nद्विषद्भिरेको बहुभिः समावृतः ।\nमहाभये सारथिमित्युवाच\nभीमश्चमूं वारयन्धार्तराष्ट्रीम् ।\nत्वं सारथे याहि जवेन वाहै-\nर्नयाम्येतान्धार्तराष्ट्रान्यमाय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, in that tumult and crush, Bhima, alone and surrounded by many foes, holding back Dhritarashtra's army in the great peril, said to his charioteer: \"Charioteer, drive the horses fast. I will send these sons of Dhritarashtra to Yama.\""}},{"n":2,"text":"संचोदितो भीमसेनेन चैवं\nस सारथिः पुत्रबलं त्वदीयम् ।\nप्रायात्ततः सारथिरुग्रवेगो\nयतो भीमस्तद्बलं गन्तुमैच्छत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Urged on by Bhimasena in this way, the charioteer drove, with fierce speed, toward your sons' army, where Bhima wished to go."}},{"n":3,"text":"ततोऽपरे नागरथाश्वपत्तिभिः\nप्रत्युद्ययुः कुरवस्तं समन्तात् ।\nभीमस्य वाहाग्र्यमुदारवेगं\nसमन्ततो बाणगणैर्निजघ्नुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then other Kurus, with elephants, chariots, horses and foot soldiers, came out against him from all sides, and struck Bhima's excellent horses, swift and powerful, with flocks of arrows on every side."}},{"n":4,"text":"ततः शरानापततो महात्मा\nचिच्छेद बाणैस्तपनीयपुङ्खैः ।\nते वै निपेतुस्तपनीयपुङ्खा\nद्विधा त्रिधा भीमशरैर्निकृत्ताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great-souled Bhima cut down the arrows as they came with gold-feathered arrows of his own, and they fell, gold-feathered, cut into two or three pieces by Bhima's shafts."}},{"n":5,"text":"ततो राजन्नागरथाश्वयूनां\nभीमाहतानां तव राजमध्ये ।\nघोरो निनादः प्रबभौ नरेन्द्र\nवज्राहतानामिव पर्वतानाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, king, a terrible roar rose in the middle of your army from the elephants, chariots, horses and young men struck down by Bhima, like mountains struck by thunderbolts."}},{"n":6,"text":"ते वध्यमानाश्च नरेन्द्रमुख्या\nनिर्भिन्ना वै भीमसेनप्रवेकैः ।\nभीमं समन्तात्समरेऽध्यरोह-\nन्वृक्षं शकुन्ता इव पुष्पहेतोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those foremost kings, being killed and pierced by Bhimasena's best arrows, still climbed up against Bhima on every side in the battle, like birds on a tree for its flowers."}},{"n":7,"text":"ततोऽभिपातं तव सैन्यमध्ये\nप्रादुश्चक्रे वेगमिवात्तवेगः ।\nयथान्तकाले क्षपयन्दिधक्षु-\nर्भूतान्तकृत्काल इवात्तदण्डः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he made a charge into your army, as swift as one given speed, like the Destroyer at the end of time, club in hand, wishing to burn and consume beings."}},{"n":8,"text":"तस्यातिवेगस्य रणेऽतिवेगं\nनाशक्नुवन्धारयितुं त्वदीयाः ।\nव्यात्ताननस्यापततो यथैव\nकालस्य काले हरतः प्रजा वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your men could not withstand the great speed of that very swift man in the battle, as no one can stand before Time, with open mouth coming to take away creatures at the appointed hour."}},{"n":9,"text":"ततो बलं भारत भारतानां\nप्रदह्यमानं समरे महात्मन् ।\nभीतं दिशोऽकीर्यत भीमनुन्नं\nमहानिलेनाभ्रगणो यथैव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, Bharata, the army of the Bharatas, being burned in the battle by that great soul, was frightened and scattered in all directions, driven by Bhima like a mass of clouds by a great wind."}},{"n":10,"text":"ततो धीमान्सारथिमब्रवीद्बली\nस भीमसेनः पुनरेव हृष्टः ।\nसूताभिजानीहि परान्स्वकान्वा\nरथान्ध्वजांश्चापततः समेतान् ।\nयुध्यन्नहं नाभिजानामि किंचि-\nन्मा सैन्यं स्वं छादयिष्ये पृषत्कैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the wise and mighty Bhimasena, cheerful again, said to his charioteer: \"Charioteer, tell which are the enemy and which our own, the chariots and banners coming together at me. In the fight I can distinguish nothing. Let me not smother my own army with arrows."}},{"n":11,"text":"अरीन्विशोकाभिनिरीक्ष्य सर्वतो\nमनस्तु चिन्ता प्रदुनोति मे भृशम् ।\nराजातुरो नागमद्यत्किरीटी\nबहूनि दुःखान्यभिजातोऽस्मि सूत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Looking around at the enemies, Vishoka, my mind is badly pained by worry. The king has not come back, sick as he is, nor has the diadem-wearer, Arjuna. I have been born to many sorrows, charioteer."}},{"n":12,"text":"एतद्दुःखं सारथे धर्मराजो\nयन्मां हित्वा यातवाञ्शत्रुमध्ये ।\nनैनं जीवन्नापि जानाम्यजीव-\nन्बीभत्सुं वा तन्ममाद्यातिदुःखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is the sorrow, charioteer: the king of dharma left me and went into the midst of the enemy. I do not know whether he is alive or dead, or Bibhatsu either. That is my great grief today."}},{"n":13,"text":"सोऽहं द्विषत्सैन्यमुदग्रकल्पं\nविनाशयिष्ये परमप्रतीतः ।\nएतान्निहत्याजिमध्ये समेता-\nन्प्रीतो भविष्यामि सह त्वयाद्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"So I, very confident, will destroy this enemy army, towering as it is. Having killed these gathered ones in the middle of the battle, I will be happy today together with you."}},{"n":14,"text":"सर्वांस्तूणीरान्मार्गणान्वान्ववेक्ष्य\nकिं शिष्टं स्यात्सायकानां रथे मे ।\nका वा जातिः किं प्रमाणं च तेषां\nज्ञात्वा व्यक्तं तन्ममाचक्ष्व सूत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Look at all the quivers and arrows and tell me what arrows remain in my chariot, of what kind and how many. Count them and tell me clearly, charioteer.\""}},{"text":"विशोक उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vishoka said:"}},{"n":15,"text":"षण्मार्गणानामयुतानि वीर\nक्षुराश्च भल्लाश्च तथायुताख्याः ।\nनाराचानां द्वे सहस्रे तु वीर\nत्रीण्येव च प्रदराणां च पार्थ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Hero, you have six ten-thousands of arrows, ten thousand each of the kshura and bhalla arrows, two thousand naracha arrows, and three thousand pradara arrows, Partha."}},{"n":16,"text":"अस्त्यायुधं पाण्डवेयावशिष्टं\nन यद्वहेच्छकटं षड्गवीयम् ।\nएतद्विद्वन्मुञ्च सहस्रशोऽपि\nगदासिबाहुद्रविणं च तेऽस्ति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pandava, there is no weapon left that a cart drawn by six oxen could not carry. Wise one, loose them by the thousand. You also have your mace, sword and strength of arm.\""}},{"text":"भीम उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhima said:"}},{"n":17,"text":"सूताद्येमं पश्य भीमप्रमुक्तैः\nसंभिन्दद्भिः पार्थिवानाशुवेगैः ।\nउग्रैर्बाणैराहवं घोररूपं\nनष्टादित्यं मृत्युलोकेन तुल्यम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Charioteer, look today at this terrible battlefield, where the sun is lost, like the world of death, with the fierce arrows of Bhima loosed, piercing kings at swift speed."}},{"n":18,"text":"अद्यैव तद्विदितं पार्थिवानां\nभविष्यति आकुमारं च सूत ।\nनिमग्नो वा समरे भीमसेन\nएकः कुरून्वा समरे विजेता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Today, charioteer, this will be known to the kings and to the world down to children: either Bhimasena sinks in the battle, or alone he conquers the Kurus."}},{"n":19,"text":"सर्वे संख्ये कुरवो निष्पतन्तु\nमां वा लोकाः कीर्तयन्त्वाकुमारम् ।\nसर्वानेकस्तानहं पातयिष्ये\nते वा सर्वे भीमसेनं तुदन्तु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let all the Kurus rush out in battle, or let the people sing of me even to children. I alone will fell them all, or let them all trouble Bhimasena."}},{"n":20,"text":"आशास्तारः कर्म चाप्युत्तमं वा\nतन्मे देवाः केवलं साधयन्तु ।\nआयात्विहाद्यार्जुनः शत्रुघाती\nशक्रस्तूर्णं यज्ञ इवोपहूतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let the gods grant me alone my hopes and the best deed. Let Arjuna, slayer of foes, come here quickly, as Indra comes to a called sacrifice."}},{"n":21,"text":"ईक्षस्वैतां भारतीं दीर्यमाणा-\nमेते कस्माद्विद्रवन्ते नरेन्द्राः ।\nव्यक्तं धीमान्सव्यसाची नराग्र्यः\nसैन्यं ह्येतच्छादयत्याशु बाणैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Look at this army of the Bharatas being torn apart. Why are these kings fleeing? Clearly the wise Savyasachin, best of men, is covering this army with arrows."}},{"n":22,"text":"पश्य ध्वजांश्च द्रवतो विशोक\nनागान्हयान्पत्तिसंघांश्च संख्ये ।\nरथान्विशीर्णाञ्शरशक्तिताडिता-\nन्पश्यस्वैतान्रथिनश्चैव सूत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Look, Vishoka, at the banners fleeing, and the elephants, horses and masses of foot soldiers in the battle. Look at these chariot-warriors and their chariots, broken and struck down by arrows and spears."}},{"n":23,"text":"आपूर्यते कौरवी चाप्यभीक्ष्णं\nसेना ह्यसौ सुभृशं हन्यमाना ।\nधनंजयस्याशनितुल्यवेगै-\nर्ग्रस्ता शरैर्बर्हिसुवर्णवाजैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Kaurava army is filled again and again, and it is being struck hard, swallowed by Dhananjaya's arrows with peacock and gold feathers, whose speed is like thunderbolts."}},{"n":24,"text":"एते द्रवन्ति स्म रथाश्वनागाः\nपदातिसंघानवमर्दयन्तः ।\nसंमुह्यमानाः कौरवाः सर्व एव\nद्रवन्ति नागा इव दावभीताः ।\nहाहाकृताश्चैव रणे विशोक\nमुञ्चन्ति नादान्विपुलान्गजेन्द्राः ॥","meaning":{"en":"These chariots, horses and elephants flee, trampling the masses of foot soldiers. All the confused Kauravas flee like elephants afraid of forest fire. And crying out in distress in the battle, Vishoka, the great elephants trumpet loudly.\""}},{"text":"विशोक उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vishoka said:"}},{"n":25,"text":"सर्वे कामाः पाण्डव ते समृद्धाः\nकपिध्वजो दृश्यते हस्तिसैन्ये ।\nनीलाद्धनाद्विद्युतमुच्चरन्तीं\nतथापश्यं विस्फुरद्वै धनुस्तत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"All your wishes are fulfilled, Pandava. The monkey banner is seen among the elephant host. I saw lightning rising from a dark cloud, and that bow flashing."}},{"n":26,"text":"कपिर्ह्यसौ वीक्ष्यते सर्वतो वै\nध्वजाग्रमारुह्य धनंजयस्य ।\nदिवाकराभो मणिरेष दिव्यो\nविभ्राजते चैव किरीटसंस्थः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That monkey is seen everywhere, sitting on the top of Dhananjaya's banner-staff. This divine jewel on his crown gleams like the sun."}},{"n":27,"text":"पार्श्वे भीमं पाण्डुराभ्रप्रकाशं\nपश्येमं त्वं देवदत्तं सुघोषम् ।\nअभीशुहस्तस्य जनार्दनस्य\nविगाहमानस्य चमूं परेषाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"At his side, Bhima, look at the Devadatta conch with its fine sound, white like a pale cloud, in the hands of Janardana as he plunges into the enemy's army."}},{"n":28,"text":"रविप्रभं वज्रनाभं क्षुरान्तं\nपार्श्वे स्थितं पश्य जनार्दनस्य ।\nचक्रं यशो वर्धयत्केशवस्य\nसदार्चितं यदुभिः पश्य वीर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Look, hero, at the discus beside Janardana, bright as the sun, with a thunderbolt hub and razor edge, which increases Keshava's fame and is always honoured by the Yadavas.\""}},{"text":"भीम उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhima said:"}},{"n":29,"text":"ददामि ते ग्रामवरांश्चतुर्दश\nप्रियाख्याने सारथे सुप्रसन्नः ।\nदसीशतं चापि रथांश्च विंशतिं\nयदर्जुनं वेदयसे विशोक ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Charioteer, I am very pleased by your good news, and I give you fourteen of the best villages, a hundred women servants, and twenty chariots, because you have told me of Arjuna, Vishoka.\""}}]}]}